    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$4.36 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for pulled pork and a three cheese sauce baked together. Very few dishes deliver this much comfort for that number.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy blocks of cheese and shred them yourself.\u003c/strong\u003e Bagged shredded cheese costs more per ounce and is coated in starch that keeps it from melting smooth. This sauce deserves better.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBraise the pork the day before.\u003c/strong\u003e The pork can sit in the fridge overnight and the assembly the next day takes 20 minutes. That is a free schedule upgrade.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eA butter and flour roux is a fraction of the cost of a cheese sauce jar.\u003c/strong\u003e Pennies of flour and a few tablespoons of butter do the same job better, and you control the salt.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eJalapeno and orange juice are the cheap flavor moves.\u003c/strong\u003e One pepper and a splash of juice cut through all that dairy for almost nothing, which is why the dish does not feel heavy."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Season the pork shoulder with salt, black pepper, ground cumin, dried oregano and dried thyme, sear it in the olive oil, then slow cook it with the diced onion, minced jalapeno, garlic and orange juice until it shreds.",
                    "Boil the pasta shells in salted water until just under al dente. They will finish in the oven, so pulling them early is the difference between good and mushy.",
                    "Melt the butter in a large pot, whisk in the flour, and cook it two minutes until it smells nutty but has not colored.",
                    "Pour in the heavy cream slowly while whisking, bring it to a bare simmer, then add the Dijon mustard and take it off the heat.",
                    "Stir in the shredded cheddar, mozzarella and Mexican cheese blend a handful at a time until the sauce is smooth, then fold in the drained pasta.",
                    "Spread half the mac in a large baking dish, layer the pulled pork across it, top with the rest of the mac, and bake at 375F for 25 minutes, then broil briefly for a browned top."
                ],
